  "source_policy": "Never mutate frozen computation. Source mismatch stops execution. Explicitly version any required runtime repair, retaining failed outputs.",
  "precompute": "Full 1400-step input sequence fixed first; generate exactly its union plus first32 HF upfront. Both target strategies and both rates use same pool, sequence and initialization within seed. Actual setup/input/target costs separate.",
  "accounting": "Not equal wall-clock. Labels shared once per seed across rates, expenses not duplicated. Training/validation/checkpoint/export and offline evaluation times recorded. Competing Python CPU>30% sampled every15s, no run exclusion.",
  "retention": "All five seeds, both rates, last+selected, ID+OOD, both endpoints. Nonfinite failures retained with missing endpoints; no replacement, additional seeds, tuning, outcome-based stopping or sample filtering. Runtime exceptions stop, retain incomplete directories for audit.",
  "analysis": "Paired corrected-minus-coarse at both endpoints/rates primary on last ID; selected and OOD secondary. Within-policy 1400-800 and target-by-update/rate interactions reported. Five-unit paired t95 descriptive, exact sign test descriptive; no multiplicity-adjusted or universal significance claim.",
  "scope": "A controlled target-strategy comparison conditional on fixed update/exposure sequence and step schedule; not a causal decomposition of old deadline gaps, not independent exposure-count mediation, not HF128 mechanism. Both endpoints share trajectories.",
  "no_test_based_choices": true
